course: dictionary
lesson: 9529
title: Stink, and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word stink usually means a very strong, bad smell. «A flower as wide as a car tyre that stinks of rotting meat» tells you the flower smells very bad, because rotting meat is the smell of something going off. Stink is also a verb, so it changes: stinks, stank, stunk. «The full bin stank by the back door for two weeks» shows the past tense.
explain: A stink can also be a noun, a thing you can name. «An engineer built huge sewers after a summer called the Great Stink.» The Great Stink was a very bad smell from the River Thames in London, so stink here is a noun for that smell. Look for words like the, a or a summer before it to spot a noun.
explain: Stink has informal meanings too. «Children say "that stinks!" when something is unfair.» Here nobody is talking about a smell. It means something is very unfair or of poor quality. In a sentence like «A girl in Edinburgh told a new boy his lunch "stinks"», the words are unkind, and the context shows the girl meant it as an insult, not a fact about food.
explain: Ask yourself which meaning fits. If the sentence is about bins, socks or rotten eggs, it means smell. If it is about fairness, a rule or a plan, it means unfair. Swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense. A dictionary can settle it when you are not sure.
fact: Stink (verb) means to have a very strong, bad smell. Its past tense is stank or stunk.
fact: A stink (noun) is a strong, bad smell, like the Great Stink in London.
fact: Informal: if something stinks, it is very bad, unfair or of poor quality.
fact: To kick up a stink, or make a stink, means to complain loudly and angrily.
fact: Phrases: stink of means to smell strongly of something; stink to high heaven means to smell very bad; stinking rich means very rich (informal).
exercise: «The full bin stank by the back door for two weeks.» What does stank mean here? | Was made of shiny metal | *Had a very strong, bad smell | Was very cold and wet | Was locked tightly
exercise: Ben says the new rule «stinks» because it is not fair. What does stinks mean here? | *Is very unfair | Is very tasty | Has a strong smell | Is very clean and new
exercise: «An engineer built huge sewers after a summer called the Great Stink.» Find and copy the word that is a noun for a strong, bad smell. | engineer | sewers | summer | *stink
test: Which phrase means to complain loudly and angrily? | A stink bomb | *To kick up a stink | To stink of rotting meat | Stinking rich
test: «Male ring-tailed lemurs have stink fights, wiping scent onto their tails and waving them at rivals.» What is a stink fight? | *A contest where lemurs wave scented tails at rivals | A fight in a smelly bin | A quarrel about who can eat the most | A game of hide and seek
exam: Which meaning fits «That rule stinks, it is so unfair»? | Very old and dusty | A smell that is very strong | Complaining loudly about a bin | *Very unfair or of poor quality
